SUMMARY:Disposable Humanity – FREE
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, November 17\, 2026 • 7 PM • Steinman Hall In Disp
 osable Humanity\, the Mitchell family—esteemed Disability Studies schola
 rs and filmmakers—delve into the chilling legacy of the Nazi Aktion T4 p
 rogram. This investigative documentary recounts the long-obscured history 
 of how over 300\,000 disabled individuals became the initial victims of th
 e Third Reich. Targeted by the T4 program as having a “life unworthy of 
 living\,” their murders laid the groundwork for the Holocaust that follo
 wed. 6:15 PM • Pre-show community panel discussion with Dr. Emily Baldys
 \, Chair of the MU Disability Film Festival\; Mr. Theo Braddy\, Executive 
 Director of the National Council on Independent Living\; Dr. Dennis Downey
 \, Disability Scholar & MU History Professor Emeritus\; Dr. Stacey Irwin\,
  Chair of the MU Holocaust & Genocide Conference Committee\; and Mr. Bob T
 ortora\, Member of the Word of Life Deaf Church. Post-show • Q&A with di
 rector Cameron Mitchell Accessibility: The film is captioned\, and live ca
 ptioning (CART) and ASL interpreting will be provided for the panel discus
 sion. Please get in touch with Barry Kornhauser to learn more. Co-presente
 d by the MU Disability Film Festival and Congregation Shaarai Shomayim. Li
 ve captioning (CART) supported by the MU Office of Learning Services.\n\nP
